SDK clock: guest durations take 1/scalar of the host time (turbo waits ran 4x long).
Phase B item B2 (docs/sdk-from-source.md). Applied by tools/build_sdk_from_source.py
(SDK_BEHAVIOUR_PATCHES). set_guest_time_scalar(s) speeds the guest tick ratio up by s,
but ScaleGuestDurationMillis / FileTime / Timeval and the XSystemClock -> WinSystemClock
cast multiplied a guest duration by s to get host time (and the reverse cast divided).
At 2x a guest Sleep(100) took ~200 ms instead of 50. Also scales relative (negative)
FILETIMEs as signed values. Behaviour at scalar 1.0 is unchanged.
The executable's old workaround (overwrite guest_time_scalar_ with 1/s,
src/core/fable2_turbo.h) probes ScaleGuestDurationMillis and stands down on this runtime.

